<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/8a7b3de7fd59> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[4143] An infamous financially motivated threat group is luring victims to a network of malware-baited sites, promising downloads of deepfake tools, according to a new report from Silent Push." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4143" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/8b65f193b31a> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Tracking FIN7 malware honeypots, new AI deepfake lures" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4142" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/91f92d427f5b> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "We observed FIN7 using two versions of the AI deepnude malware honeypots: 1 that requires a simple download and the other that has a sophisticated “free trial” process." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4144" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/950bcbe81002> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[4141] Zach Edwards of the cybersecurity firm Silent Push said that the Russian group Fin7 seems to be behind several websites that use variations of the name \"AINude.ai\" to trick their mostly male victims into giving them their info without their knowledge." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4141" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/97b6eb478c65> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[4142] 1 of the most recent FIN7 malware delivery lures is being used across several domains and promotes 'AI Deepfake Nude Generating Software', which leads to D3F@ck Loader and at least one additional payload." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4142" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/999406856ab7> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[4143] An infamous financially motivated threat group is luring victims to a network of malware-baited sites, promising downloads of deepfake tools, according to a new report from Silent Push." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4143" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/a3be30448a5b> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Silent Push is also tracking the FIN7 NetSupport RAT malvertising campaign, which continues to use a different honeypot with “Browser extension required” pop-up lures that lead to .MSIX malware." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4144" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/ab02fa0bfba5> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "aiNude[.]ai Deepnude Generator click “free trial” offering honeypot" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4144" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/b29ccf1948cb> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[4143] An infamous financially motivated threat group is luring victims to a network of malware-baited sites, promising downloads of deepfake tools, according to a new report from Silent Push." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4143" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/bb1d1bed03a0> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Silent Push research has revealed that FIN7’s current attack strategy uses different honeypots: AI adult-based generator malware and a continuing NetSupport remote access Trojan (RAT)." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4144" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/bb3d4c22a2ba> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[4141] \"The deepfake AI software may have an audience of mostly men with a decent amount who use other AI software or have crypto accounts,\" Edwards told 404." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4141" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/bc20318d6de1> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Our team found AI Deepfake honeypots are built atop “shell websites” used by FIN7 for aging domains (sites later modified to deploy malware or execute malicious campaigns)." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4144" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/c916b752830e> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The sites, many under the brandname aiNude.ai, embed a Trojan or infostealer in a web extension or other file that users are directed to download." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4145" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/f0721b3072f2> a airo:Evidence ;
